   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I need to be able to determine which shiny object has most recently changed, on the server side. For instance, I have a data table displaying some search results linked to two different text inputs. For aesthetic reasons, I would like to avoid having a data table for each input. Instead I would like to detect which text input has most recently changed and update the table accordingly. <div><br></div><div>For example:</div><div><br></div><div>output$my.table &lt;- renderDataTable({ <br></div><div>   input$a</div><div>   input$b</div><div>   if( mostRecent(input$a) ) {</div><div>      ... do something</div><div>   } else {</div><div>      ... do something else </div><div>  }</div><div>})</div><div><br></div><div>Any idea how to solve this that doesn&#39;t use a global, shared variable that tracks which one fired most recently?</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "mljUnHNO3mQJ",
