    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Well, it will you whta you want, see also <a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/tutorial/lesson6/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/tutorial/lesson6/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792402569302000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0E18m48Bc27pqlY8PIeXkM\">http://shiny.rstudio.com/tutorial/lesson6/</a> <br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">  lastA </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> reactive</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>     input$a<br>     </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sys</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">time</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>  lastB </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> reactive</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>     input$b<br>     </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sys</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">time</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>  output$my</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">table </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> renderDataTable</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>     lasta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lastA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>     lastb </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lastB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>     </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lasta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lastb</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># check how time comparisons can be done R correctly</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>       </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># b was changed last</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>     </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> elseif </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lasta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lastb</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>       </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># a was changed last</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>     </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><br>Shiny\r\n knows that my.table depends on input$a and input$b. If either of them \r\nis changed then renderDataTable must be run. However, if input$a is \r\nchanged then lastA() will be run, it may deliver a new result. Since \r\ninput$b has not been changed shiny does not run lastB() again (it is a \r\nreactive expression!), but it delivers the (stored) result from the last \r\ntime when lastB() has been really run; which actually is the last change of input$b. As result in both routines deliver\r\n the last time when input$a and input$b has changed such that you can \r\neasily compare them.<br><br>I guess that is what you want. Best Sigbert<br></div>"
